WEBVTT

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.160
You're certain it was a Factory prison van?

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.710
I'm positive. And Miho and the others weren't working a case last night.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.130
What's Zaizen started?

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:20.980
Amon... How much did you learn about Zaizen at headquarters?

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.680
His objectives, I mean.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.590
It isn't about Witch hunts using Orbo?

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.690
That's only half of it.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:36.860
His real objective is to use Orbo to let ordinary humans hunt Witches.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:44.030
Zaizen has put that project into action.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:48.370
Now that you mention it, there's been a sudden spike in Factory activity.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.010
You've been looking into this?

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.010
I've had my eye on them.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.640
But there's one thing I don't understand.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.150
Why is headquarters afraid of that?

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.260
I wouldn't think that using normal humans to hunt Witches...

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.990
...goes against Solomon's ideology.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:09.560
You're planning to stake them out?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.770
We need to find out whether or not the Factory has started...

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:15.570
...using Orbo that can be used by humans.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:17.700
I see.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.110
Where are you going?

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:23.740
To try to get confirmation. If anything happens, call me.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.210
You're in no position to order me around...

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.750
Don't worry. I'll be sure to call you.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.890
Man, what am I gonna do about this guy?

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.610
"August 30th."

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.600
"At long last, the truth lies before us."

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.940
"This tiny mutation is the Devil's true form."

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.850
"October 5th."

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:06.310
"I fear I may have been committing a grave mistake."

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.360
"God had already left us."

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.000
I wonder what was written here?

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.170
What was he doing with Juliano?

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.070
It's morning already?

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.640
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:57.370
...the instant I look away.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.510
I just kept counting...

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:07.950
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:15.320
...that I'd vomited up.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:21.260
In this time that seems so dry,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.370
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:32.230
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:35.280
...and tears them to pieces.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:44.950
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:52.780
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.710
Apparently, there was an intensive genetic research program...

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:19.010
...being conducted at Solomon HQ's research facility at one point.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.730
At Solomon?

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.260
But there's been a huge boom in genetic research...

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.250
...all over the world these past few years, right?

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:34.230
It's hardly surprising that an organization with Solomon's financial muscle got involved, too.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.740
Only if their goal was the same as other research agencies.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:39.300
What do you mean?

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:43.910
Apparently, Solomon succeeded in mapping the human genome...

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.440
...more than five years before any other research agency.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.480
However, the research project was disbanded right afterwards...

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:53.250
...without their findings ever being published.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:55.820
It was an action by Solomon, right?

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.090
I can understand why they wouldn't go public,

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:01.200
...but why was the project itself suddenly aborted?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.820
See what I mean? Strange, huh?

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:04.390
Think it's related to Orbo?

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:07.570
Yes! That's what I thought, too.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.870
So what you're saying is that headquarters attacked us...

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.360
...because they don't approve of Orbo development, Michael?

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.910
It's not like I have any hard evidence,

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:19.880
...but after digging around here and there, I have to come to that conclusion.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:24.150
But what makes them hate the very idea of Orbo?

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:25.510
Beats me.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:30.450
But if you think about it, we ourselves don't know anything about Orbo.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.380
Now that you mention it, you have a point.

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:34.090
Say...

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:40.100
No, forget it.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:41.360
I just...

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:46.000
I was thinking that if it really was HQ that attacked us,

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:52.470
...that means we're using something that they'll go to extreme lengths to make us stop using.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.420
Stop that, you're freaking me out.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:56.380
Right?

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.330
Hey! How long are you going to stay in bed, you juvenile delinquent?!

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.820
Good morning.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:33.780
I'd hardly call this morning! Do you know what time it is?!

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:42.890
- Oh, no. I overslept.
- Where's the boss?

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.220
- Boss?
- You two were out until all hours, right?

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.400
I know all about it.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.600
I don't know.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.370
Is that the truth?

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:54.430
I don't know.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:59.780
Darn it, we've got clients coming in soon!

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:04.280
Hirata! Go check at the International Center!

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.360
You really don't know?

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:19.860
I don't know!

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:25.190
International Center

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:25.190
International Center

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:25.190
International Center

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:25.190
International Center

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:41.260
So she burned the guy's hair off?

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.480
She sure did!

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:46.290
If she's not wearing her glasses, she'll set just about anything on fire!

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.190
Considering that he's your big brother, this geezer's pretty cool, Amon.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.530
Who are you calling a geezer?

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:58.800
Well, go ahead and continue last night's little heart-to-heart.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.330
I'll get out of your hair.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:02.470
Buh-bye!

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:05.150
See you, Yurika!

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:07.550
You, me, and Robin oughta have a barbecue...

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.930
Looks like this is getting even more complicated than I thought.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.960
For the time being, the Japan branch isn't showing any overt activity.

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.770
Seeing which way the wind blows, hm?

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.570
In any case, they're bound to show some activity soon enough.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.780
If anything happens, contact me immediately.

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:42.920
Yes, sir. Also, according to the intelligence division's report,

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:47.980
...the source of the system intrusion the other day was definitely the STN-J.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.150
I see.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.020
What would you like us to do?

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:55.590
I'll deal with it. But keep them under close surveillance.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.120
Understood, sir.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.700
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.190
Not at all, sir.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:04.240
From what you told me,

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:07.900
...am I to understand that the damage was caused by a sort of mismatch?

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.070
Yes, sir.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.480
We believe that there is a rejection between the character of the test subject...

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.950
...and lingering traces of Witch individuality present in the Orbo,

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.150
...resulting in the manifestation of the symptoms we have seen.

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:20.640
Is there any way to confirm this?

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:24.320
Not if we don't get a little more clinical data.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:27.550
You're saying that we should continue human testing?

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:29.660
They aren't the same as Witches.

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:31.600
But sir...

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.660
At any rate, I'll restrict Orbo usage to known safe levels for the time being.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:42.870
Even with that, our results ought to be enough to shut up that bunch that's raising a stink.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:44.670
Y- Yes, sir.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.150
If you'll excuse me...

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:57.750
I suppose I shouldn't waste any time in dealing with this matter, either.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:05.530
Do you still hate Dad?

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:08.360
Our father?

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.570
I'd be lying if I said that I wasn't bitter,

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:16.940
...but I suppose you can't hold a grudge for years against a man you've never seen.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.940
I'd forgotten all about him until you brought him up.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:22.670
Your mother, then?

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:29.710
She's a complete stranger to me, but she seemed like a really nice lady.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.060
Even if she was a Seed.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:38.660
Is it because your father... the man your mother chose to be your father... was a Witch?

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:45.100
She was...

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.530
She was always kind to me.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.380
The life of a Seed never seemed that bad to me.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:56.510
Even if my real father wasn't there, it was enough so long as she was with me.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:59.490
But I was wrong.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:00.820
That little incident, huh?

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:02.960
That woman, she...

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:07.520
Mother awakened as a Witch for him right in front of my eyes.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:12.160
I couldn't get through to her anymore.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:16.930
And that's why you hate your mother... no, Witches.

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:19.700
I doubt you'd understand.

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:23.810
You wouldn't understand the fear that her blood that's lying dormant inside of me...

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:27.580
...could suddenly awaken at any moment, just like hers did.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:31.820
Because I'm human?

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:37.280
Witches, Seeds, whatever you call 'em, keep showing up at my door for some reason,

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:41.550
...but they don't look any different from humans to me.

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:46.160
Besides, I have Dad's blood in me, same as you.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:50.500
It's not just a question of saying, "That person's a Witch," or, "That guy isn't," right?

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.770
Your mother chose Dad.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:57.610
Doesn't that show how much she loved him?

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.950
So, what are you going to do about the girl?

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:12.250
Hey, YOU were the one who asked me to help her.

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:17.020
I thought you'd finally realized that.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.190
The situation has changed since then.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.170
What situation?

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:26.500
She... There's a secret that Robin knows that we don't.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.980
A secret, huh?

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:33.340
That was the trail they sent you to follow?

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:37.950
But I get the feeling that Robin herself doesn't know what that secret is.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:39.780
Just as I thought...

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:41.590
Why the hesitation?

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:46.250
Robin is being chased by Solomon and she doesn't know why.

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:50.800
To hunt her, I have to know. I have to know the truth.

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:56.270
And if you find out, will you be able to hunt her?

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:59.270
The way she is now, you're no match for Robin.

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:00.440
I know that!

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:03.410
But I have to find the answer.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:16.250
Get going.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:18.650
Robin's too much for me to handle now.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.550
I'm giving her back to you.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.440
H-Hey, what do you think you're doing?!

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:44.350
You're tailing Amon, right?

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:45.650
Wrong answer.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.890
I guess you can't trust a lawyer's intuition, either.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:51.080
Hey, don't talk like that!

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.320
Where are you going, then?

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:55.290
The Factory.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.160
Factory?

00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:59.020
What do you wanna do? Want out?

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.990
Nah, hit it.

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:07.970
I'm heading home. How about you, Ms. Karasuma?

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:10.670
I'm going to do a little more digging.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.210
I'll see if the police know anything.

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:15.650
I don't think it'll do any good.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:17.080
Just in case.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:19.490
Well, if you say so. Good night.

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:21.180
Later, Michael.

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:22.790
Yeah.

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:31.230
I guess...

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:35.000
I guess I'll go ask about that picture...

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:38.700
Nagira might have gone over there to do some digging, too...

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.180
Nagira?

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:55.080
If you use your Craft, you could incinerate me before I could shoot.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.090
Amon...

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:18.010
I can't believe you'd do something this illegal. This organization of yours is...

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:20.110
It's not my organization.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:25.140
You saved me back then.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.520
That may have been a mistake.

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:30.890
You think I'm a Witch?

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:33.520
That's what headquarters believes.

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:35.490
What do you believe, Amon?

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:40.800
I was ordered by someone at Solomon headquarters to hunt you.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:44.840
By the most influential hunter trainer at Solomon.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:49.170
By the man who raised you, Juliano Colegli.

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:51.940
He was the one who ordered the hunt!

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:53.680
You're lying...

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:55.470
It's no lie.

00:15:55.820 --> 00:16:00.340
The Father gave me the order in firm, unwavering words.

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:04.150
"Robin has gained dangerous power through the Craft Arcanum."

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.250
"She must be hunted."

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.790
That can't be... The Father would never...

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:13.470
That's...

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:20.860
Amon, that was you?

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:26.850
If I hadn't read this letter that day, I might not have saved you.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:30.740
I can read it?

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:40.260
Father... But this is a...

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:42.920
A confession written to one who is about to die.

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:45.390
At first, I couldn't understand, either.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:49.430
What is written in there is a jumbled mix of fear and love.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.330
And regret.

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:56.000
Juliano is afraid of me? But why?

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:58.610
How could he be afraid of me?

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:00.880
When I stood across from him at headquarters,

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:03.480
...I was filled with an indescribable feeling that something didn't add up.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:08.420
What could explain the discrepancy between what is in that letter...

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:11.290
...and the priest who coldly spelled out the reason for your hunt?

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:15.460
The Arcanum gave you dangerous power?

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:19.260
I'll admit that in the letter, the Father was afraid of something.

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:24.940
But on the contrary, I got the impression that his fear was directed at your very existence.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.140
My existence?

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:31.410
To see for myself where the Father's true intentions lay,

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:35.270
...I began to pursue Toudou's tracks... your past.

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:39.210
That Toudou man has something to do with my past?

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:48.200
Amon, if you can't have faith in me... If you think that I'm a dangerous Witch...

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.220
Go ahead.

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:54.030
I have faith in your heart, Amon.

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:08.010
I suppose this is my answer.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:11.050
Your answer, Amon?

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:15.450
What is it?

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:19.380
Amon? They're on the move.

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.620
They just left the gate.

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:22.900
I see.

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:26.090
Follow them. I'll meet up with you soon.

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:28.130
Did something happen?

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:29.590
It's the Factory.

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:31.370
The Factory?

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:32.930
An assault team just left.

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:34.630
You coming?

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.940
A minute ago, one of the vans went off in another direction.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:44.680
The one we're following seems to be tailing a bike.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:47.210
I wonder if they'll keep going towards the coast?

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:48.710
Our location is...

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:56.660
Hunting Witches without using hunters? That's what Zaizen is trying to do?

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:59.930
Solomon HQ is nervous about his activities, as well.

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:02.630
Without using hunters...

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:06.100
But that would mean that hunters won't be...

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:39.800
No way! Sakaki?!

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:42.070
Why are they after Sakaki?!

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:43.810
Oh, crap!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:49.720
Robin?

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:57.090
Sakaki? Why is the Factory after a hunter?

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:02.720
Ow...

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:09.290
Amon...!

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:33.120
Wait.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:48.810
Why did you let them go?

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:51.110
We know where they came from.

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:54.950
Plus, they seemed to be having some problems.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.480
And on top of that...

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:57.750
Oh, no! I forgot!

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:01.450
Hey there.

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:04.950
Nagira? What are you...

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.550
I guess this means you two came to an understanding.

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:12.930
Are you okay?

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:15.230
Crap... What the hell was that all about?

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:17.830
That was a Factory assault team.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:21.040
That's my point! Why would the Factory attack me?!

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:23.640
Hey, I don't know, either!

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:27.410
Huh? Dojima? What are you doing?

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.680
Amon? And Robin, too?

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:32.810
What's going on?!

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:34.520
I'll explain later.

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:38.020
The real question is, why would the Factory attack you?

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:39.720
Karasuma?

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:42.730
Sakaki, where's Karasuma?

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:46.630
She said she was gonna leave a little after I did.

00:22:36.920 --> 00:22:44.910
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:47.770
Tell me.

00:22:48.980 --> 00:22:59.760
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:09.650
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.330 --> 00:23:14.140
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:19.510
...all those promises...

00:23:21.450 --> 00:23:25.910
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:31.710
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:40.490
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
